## Science sources

- [NASA Mars Facts](https://science.nasa.gov/mars/facts/) supports planet order, size, surface, atmosphere, volcanoes, canyons and the length of a day.
- [NASA Perseverance landing site](https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/landing/mission/landing_site/) supports the ancient lake and delta and the search for potential signs of ancient microbial life.
- [NASA Perseverance science highlights](https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/science-highlights/) supports the water evidence and rock investigation. A habitable environment is not proof of life.
- The three records above support the photography, instruments and captions. The English student text is adapted from the supplied reader.
